  "verse": "And know that whatever you do which is unright, it will come back on you; and battle (war) also belongs to unright and great terribleness and you shall avoid it with all good and fair (responsible) means as well as with love… consider, battle (war) is never a way to the creation of peace, freedom, love and consonance (harmony) amongst all peoples of your kind (humankind), but only a way of mishappening, hatred, unpeace, unfreedom (bondage), dissonance (disharmony), pillage, revenge and retaliation, robbery, destruction and boundless outrage with bloody deeds (killing) and defilement (violation)…",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 8, Verse 42",
  "hinge": "The cause is not the hack and it is not the missiles. It is the choice — by Ukraine's digital ministry, whether civilian-warning infrastructure is hardened and given redundant, verifiable fallbacks or remains one app with one server; by Russia, whether a fake nuclear alert inside Ukraine is counted as an achievement or as an attack on civilians that invites the same in return; by the US and Europe, whether 500 interceptors promised \"several years\" out is a policy or an excuse; and by both armies, whether the Kherson model — a named humanitarian purpose, a fixed window, a corridor that held — is repeated. §8:42 says war produces pillage, revenge and retaliation and nothing else; the Kherson weekend shows what a *limited* agreement can do, which is exactly why the limit is the thing being chosen."
